{
 "name": "c48",
 "description": "Driven cable car C6. Two beam-brick wall pods straddle the cord, tied at the top by two rope axles and cross\nbricks. 43 mm tyres everywhere: deck wheels on the pods, one free tyre on each rope axle above the cord (bottoms 80 mm\nabove the deck-wheel bottoms = the cord top at the saddles), the rope axles 8 mm ahead of the deck axles so each\nrope wheel takes the cord before its deck wheel leaves the start deck and keeps it until its deck wheel is on the\ngoal deck. Drive is continuous: two L motors drive the rear deck wheels (start and goal decks), an M motor on top of\nthe left pod drives the rear rope axle (the cord) at the same surface speed. AAA boxes sandwiched low in both pods\nkeep the centre of mass well below the cord.",
 "part_set": "inventory",
 "chassis": "H0L",
 "motor": "motorL",
